Package: aurora-speaker-upgrade
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-cryptography, util-linux, alsa-utils, systemd, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: speakerguardd-v2, lzfse
Description: Move the speakers to speakerguardd v2 with this Mac's own tuning
 aurora-speaker-upgrade moves an installed Mac's speakers from the legacy
 protection (speakersafetyd, speakerguardd 0.1) to speakerguardd v2 with the
 Mac's own tuning, and back (--revert). It collects the installer's tuning
 bundle, stores it root-only, lets v2's silent self-check prove it, and
 switches the kernel's speaker interface only on a pass. The legacy stack
 stays installed and keeps any Mac whose self-check refuses.
 .
 On Aurora Debian the switch is opt in: the boot unit, which runs the same
 switch at every boot, is installed disabled. The legacy protection is
 deprecated; while it holds the speakers, a notice at login asks the user to
 try speakerguardd v2 and report the result. Reading Apple's LZFSE-compressed
 restore images needs the lzfse library.
